            <ArticleTitle>The relationship between acute coronary syndrome and sildenafil.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1424.e1-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.ajem.2013.05.019</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0735-6757(13)00294-5</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Sildenafil is a drug used for male erectile dysfunction. Sildenafil's fatal cardiac effects except due to hypotension with simultaneous nitrate use have not been reported.We reported in this case a 70-year-old man admitted to the emergency service with chest pain, which occurs in an hour after sildenafil use. Electrocardiogram showed inferoposterior ST-segment elevation. In angiography, total circumflex artery occlusion has been seen.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
